devfreq: wilkbook_dmc — static-low DDR frequency for the PineNote (rk3566)

A minimal devfreq driver around the Rockchip DRAM SIP (SMC 0x82000008),
holding DDR at the firmware table's lowest rate for the life of the boot.
The SMC sequences are transplanted verbatim from the hardware-proven test
module (pinenote/tools/ddr-dvfs-test/src/ddr-dvfs-test.c; BSP citations in
pinenote/tools/ddr-dvfs-test/protocol.md): share-mem 2 pages -> zero ->
DRAM_INIT -> GET_FREQ_INFO at probe; SET_RATE with the MCU deferral path
(a1 == -6 -> MCU_START -> 100 ms sleep -> POST_SET_RATE) and a GET_RATE
verify for every switch.

MEASURED, on this device (doc/artifacts/pinenote-awake-levers-20260806):
  - DDR ATF version 0x101; firmware table 324/528/780/1056 MHz (the TPL
    trained all four setpoints);
  - 324 vs 1056 MHz saves ~24.8 mA in the quiesced bracketed pair
    (174.4 vs 199.2 mA battery drain, same boot, unplugged);
  - a switch costs ~107 ms wall on the MCU path, sub-ms actual DRAM
    stall; memory intact (first switch in this board's history,
    2026-08-06);
  - bl31 PRESERVES a non-boot rate across deep suspend/resume, proven on
    both resumes of the addendum-2 audit -- ddr_after=324 following D1
    and D2.

ASSUMED (bounded, not measured):
  - the firmware behaves for any table entry <= the boot rate, not just
    324 (targets are restricted to exact GET_FREQ_INFO entries via the
    OPP set, the BSP's own discipline; under powersave only 324 is ever
    requested);
  - the share-page re-request on re-probe returns the boot-time region
    (BSP-documented behavior, protocol.md par.1, exercised by the test
    module's insmod/rmmod cycles).

Design decisions carried into code:
  - NO dev_pm_ops, NO opp-suspend, zero switches around suspend.  This
    explicitly OVERRIDES the earlier design doc's conservative
    restore-before-suspend rule: the addendum-2 audit measured bl31
    carrying a non-boot rate through suspend/resume twice, so suspend
    hooks would only add switches (and EBC exposure) for nothing.
  - Firmware is the single source of truth for rates: dynamic OPPs from
    GET_FREQ_INFO, no DT OPP table.  Nothing above the boot rate is
    registered (no OPP voltage scaling on this rail; boot voltage was
    chosen for 1056 MHz), and target() refuses it besides.
  - Built =m with the powersave governor: the ONLY runtime switch is the
    probe-time drop to 324 MHz, so the pinenote-dmc loader service owns
    switch timing and quiesces fbcon around modprobe (a switch stalls
    every AXI master; a stall inside an active EBC frame risks the 25 ms
    EBC_FRAME_TIMEOUT and terminal poison -- protocol.md par.4).  rmmod
    restores the boot rate; the operator quiesces the display first.
  - probe refuses politely (-ENODEV, no devfreq) if the firmware version
    is below 0x101 or the table is empty, so a foreign or downgraded
    bl31 costs a log line, not a broken boot.

The dmc DT node carries only the compatible and status: the driver's one
conduit is the SMC, and policy lives in the firmware table.

Acceptance (next boot): /sys/class/devfreq/*/cur_freq == 324000000 with
governor powersave, clk_scmi_ddr == 324000000 in clk_summary with the
reader running, rate still 324 after one deep cycle, dmesg free of
wilkbook_dmc errors.

Applies on top of (in kernel.scm order): linux-pinenote-7.0-forward-port,
-bsp-sip-probe, -st-accel-pm, -cpuidle-psci, -vdd-cpu-auto-pfm.

